(4467570, 639881, 50695, '<td valign="top">Wow. That''s tremendous. The composition and the processing put a lot of emphasis on the architecture. It''s a classic architecture shot. And a painting as well. Beautiful to look at.</td>', 'Wow. That''s tremendous. The composition and the processing put a lot of emphasis on the architecture. It''s a classic architecture shot. And a painting as well. Beautiful to look at.', '2008-02-07 08:33:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4467575, 639881, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by amathiasphoto:</b></div><hr/><i>Also, the people are the darkest part, and with this supposed to be focusing on architecture, I think that there is to much focus on them. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Architecture is for people. To show people in an architectural space is of supreme relevance.</td>', 'Originally posted by amathiasphoto:Also, the people are the darkest part, and with this supposed to be focusing on architecture, I think that there is to much focus on them.   Architecture is for people. To show people in an architectural space is of supreme relevance.', '2008-02-07 08:36:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4467790, 638089, 811, '<td valign="top">I like this shot.  the house color contrasts nicely with the sky.  I would have expected a higher score than that, honestly -- high fives, low sixes to be honest.  Maybe a tighter crop, though I''m not exactly sure what you could crop out.</td>', 'I like this shot.  the house color contrasts nicely with the sky.  I would have expected a higher score than that, honestly -- high fives, low sixes to be honest.  Maybe a tighter crop, though I''m not exactly sure what you could crop out.', '2008-02-07 09:47:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4467840, 639602, 14437, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Haneck:</b></div><hr/><i> Well... unfortunately the first thing that caught my eye was the jagged, pixely lines of the lights. But when I really looked at it and tried to imagine it without the jagged lines... I realized this would probably be a glorious photo. The kind that, as <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=65234" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">MaryO</a> mentioned down below, makes your jaw drop because it''s so inexplicably fantastic. Wonderful! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Only now I notice the jagged line.<br/>I think the problem is with the resize software. When I shoot and post this photo, I was actually at oversea and don''t have Photoshop with me. I have to use the hotel''s PC to resize this shot and summit it before the due date. The only software available in the hotel''s PC is Microsoft Office Photo Editor or something like that. I couldn''t even do any curve. All I did was just rotate and resize.<br/>Anyway, I''m glad that you guys like it :)</td>', 'Originally posted by Haneck: Well... unfortunately the first thing that caught my eye was the jagged, pixely lines of the lights. But when I really looked at it and tried to imagine it without the jagged lines... I realized this would probably be a glorious photo. The kind that, as  MaryO mentioned down below, makes your jaw drop because it''s so inexplicably fantastic. Wonderful!  Only now I notice the jagged line.I think the problem is with the resize software. When I shoot and post this photo, I was actually at oversea and don''t have Photoshop with me. I have to use the hotel''s PC to resize this shot and summit it before the due date. The only software available in the hotel''s PC is Microsoft Office Photo Editor or something like that. I couldn''t even do any curve. All I did was just rotate and resize.Anyway, I''m glad that you guys like it :)', '2008-02-07 10:01:43.000000', NULL, 0),
